### =====================================================================
### END-TO-END (Phase 7): the order saga, through the API gateway (port 8080)
###
###   POST /orders -> order PENDING + OrderCreated
###     -> inventory reserves the stock (StockReserved)     -> cart removes the items, counts the coupon
###     -> payment: COD accepted (PaymentConfirmed)  |  ONLINE: the customer pays -> PaymentConfirmed / PaymentFailed
###     -> order CONFIRMED -> store accepts, packs, hands over -> the delivery partner picks it up and delivers it
###   Cancel / reject -> stock released, a paid order refunded (RefundCompleted)
###
### Needs: infrastructure, auth, customer, store, product-read, inventory, cart, order, payment, delivery, api-gateway,
###        and the connectors (scripts\register-connectors.ps1).
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Run the requests IN ORDER.
### "wait" steps: each saga step travels through Kafka (outbox -> Debezium -> Kafka -> consumer), about a second each.
### =====================================================================

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080

@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@customer2Token = {{customer2Login.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@vendorToken = {{vendorLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@partnerToken = {{partnerLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@deliveryId = {{partnerDelivery.response.body.$.data.content[0].id}}
@codOrderId = {{codOrder.response.body.$.data.id}}
@onlineOrderId = {{onlineOrder.response.body.$.data.id}}
@failedOrderId = {{failedOrder.response.body.$.data.id}}
@rejectedOrderId = {{rejectedOrder.response.body.$.data.id}}


### 1. customer1 (user 4) logs in
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 2. customer2 (user 7) logs in
# @name customer2Login
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer2@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 3. vendor1 (Fresh Mart, store 1) logs in
# @name vendorLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vendor1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 4. The admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 5. delivery1 (Arjun Singh, user 5, zone Indiranagar) logs in
# @name partnerLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "delivery1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### ===== A. Cash on delivery, all the way to DELIVERED =====


### 6. customer1's seed cart (Fresh Mart, 201.00) with coupon SAVE10 -> 20.10 off, payable 210.90
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/coupon
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "SAVE10"
}


### 7. Place the order: COD to the HOME address (1) -> 201, status PENDING
# @name codOrder
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": 1,
  "paymentMethod": "COD",
  "note": "Please ring the bell twice"
}


### 8. (wait) Stock reserved + COD accepted -> CONFIRMED, payment CASH_ON_DELIVERY, timeline has 2 steps
# @wait 4
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{codOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 9. The cart was emptied by OrderCreated (cart-service)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 10. Search shows the reserved stock: Tomato 120 -> 118 available
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products?q=tomato
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 11. vendor1's new orders (CONFIRMED) -> the order is waiting
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders?status=CONFIRMED
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 12. vendor1 accepts it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{codOrderId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 13. ...packs it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{codOrderId}}/pack
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 14. ...and hands it over
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{codOrderId}}/ready-for-pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 15. (wait) delivery1 goes online -> delivery-service assigns the waiting delivery to them (DeliveryAssigned)
# @wait 3
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/online
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 16. delivery1's current delivery: ASSIGNED, pickup at Fresh Mart, drop at the customer's address
# @name partnerDelivery
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries?active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 17. delivery1 accepts it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 18. ...collects it at the store (DeliveryPickedUp -> order OUT_FOR_DELIVERY)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/pick-up
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 19. (wait) The order is OUT_FOR_DELIVERY and shows deliveryPartnerName "Arjun Singh"
# @wait 3
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{codOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 20. Cancel now -> 400 "An order that is OUT_FOR_DELIVERY can no longer be cancelled"
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{codOrderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 21. ...starts the trip
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/start
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 22. ...and delivers it (DeliveryCompleted -> order DELIVERED, paymentStatus PAID: the cash was collected)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 23. (wait) payment-service: COLLECTED
# @wait 4
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{codOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ===== B. Online payment, paid, then cancelled -> refund =====


### 24. customer1 adds 2 dozen bananas (120.00)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 4,
  "quantity": 2
}


### 25. Place the order ONLINE -> PENDING
# @name onlineOrder
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": 1,
  "paymentMethod": "ONLINE"
}


### 26. (wait) Stock reserved -> the payment waits for the customer: AWAITING_PAYMENT, canPayNow true
# @wait 4
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{onlineOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 27. Pay with the mock gateway -> PAID
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{onlineOrderId}}/mock-pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "success": true
}


### 28. (wait) The order is CONFIRMED, paymentStatus PAID
# @wait 3
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{onlineOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 29. The customer cancels it -> CANCELLED
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{onlineOrderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Ordered by mistake"
}


### 30. (wait) Compensation: the payment is REFUNDED (refundReference mock_refund_...)
# @wait 4
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{onlineOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 31. ...and the order shows paymentStatus REFUNDED
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{onlineOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ===== C. Online payment declined -> the order is cancelled =====


### 32. customer1 adds 1 kg of Shimla apples (162.00)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 5,
  "quantity": 1
}


### 33. Place the order ONLINE
# @name failedOrder
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": 1,
  "paymentMethod": "ONLINE"
}


### 34. (wait) The bank declines the payment (mock)
# @wait 4
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{failedOrderId}}/mock-pay
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "success": false
}


### 35. (wait) -> CANCELLED by SYSTEM "Payment failed: ...", paymentStatus FAILED (stock released)
# @wait 4
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{failedOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### ===== D. The store rejects an order =====


### 36. customer2 (user 7) adds 3 x Lay's (60.00) and 1 x Surf Excel (195.50) from Fresh Mart
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 9,
  "quantity": 3
}


### 37. ...
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 10,
  "quantity": 1
}


### 38. Place the order COD to customer2's HOME address (3, PIN 560008)
# @name rejectedOrder
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": 3,
  "paymentMethod": "COD"
}


### 39. (wait) vendor1 rejects it -> REJECTED (stock released, payment cancelled)
# @wait 4
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{rejectedOrderId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Surf Excel is damaged, sorry"
}


### 40. (wait) customer2 sees the reason in the timeline
# @wait 3
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{rejectedOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}


### 41. (wait) payment-service: CANCELLED (nothing was paid)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/payments/orders/{{rejectedOrderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}


### ===== E. Problems are caught before the order exists =====


### 42. customer2 adds 1 x Amul Butter (56.00)
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 7,
  "quantity": 1
}


### 43. Amul Butter alone (56.00) is below the minimum order value -> 409 with the problem in "errors"
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": 3,
  "paymentMethod": "COD"
}


### 44. My order history (customer1): 3 orders, newest first
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 45. Admin: every cancelled order
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/orders?status=CANCELLED
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 46. Admin: refunds
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/payments?status=REFUNDED
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 47. CLEAN UP: customer2 empties the cart
DELETE {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customer2Token}}
